# Sources for searched replies: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# (info and bestmove), fisher-2aj rules 1, 7 and 10, and python-chess 1.11.2
# for the independently checked exact values. Written 2026-11-23.
# UCI position and go.
> position fen 7k/8/5KQ1/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. Qg7 is the only move that gives checkmate in one.
# Python-chess counts 23, 15, 373 and 840 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 4 score mate 1 nodes 1251
# UCI bestmove. The unique mate in one fixes the move.
< bestmove g6g7
# UCI quit.
> quit
! exit
